WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.722
APEX: ensemble-based history matching, forecasting, uncertainty quantification and optimization of subsurface models.

2
00:00:10.722 --> 00:00:16.235
It natively re-implements and extends NORCE's Python Ensemble Toolbox (PET).

3
00:00:16.235 --> 00:00:22.256
APEX is compatible with ERT: with APEX's interface, each can run the other's cases.

4
00:00:22.256 --> 00:00:30.687
PET and ERT cases convert to and from APEX cases, within what each can express.

5
00:00:30.687 --> 00:00:35.921
With OPM Flow, APEX history-matches the 3dBox case on its rates and seismic maps.

6
00:00:35.921 --> 00:00:44.114
Commercial simulators (Eclipse) are used when installed and licensed on your machine.

7
00:00:44.114 --> 00:01:02.545
A run's folder holds provenance.json (the APEX commit, the libraries, the host and the inputs' hashes that made it).

8
00:01:02.545 --> 00:01:10.936
Inside: geostatistical and facies priors, MCP, the runtime agents' model providers (tools for LLMs) and eCalc.

9
00:01:10.936 --> 00:01:12.843
From Python: import apex.

10
00:01:12.843 --> 00:01:19.967
The parity tests compare against stored reference results.

11
00:01:19.967 --> 00:01:33.011
The web UI and its AI assistant: give the assistant a model (Claude through Claude Code with your subscription, or Gemma through Ollama), a hosted or a local LLM.

12
00:01:33.011 --> 00:01:36.247
And agents that plan, monitor and report on the work.

13
00:01:36.247 --> 00:01:46.578
Bringing your own case: the case-converter and the geomodeler turn a deck and its history into an APEX case, give it a prior.

14
00:01:46.578 --> 00:01:52.078
Writing and registering your own plugin.

15
00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.643
Status: early development.

16
00:01:53.643 --> 00:01:59.051
Get the code, and start with the Quick start.

17
00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:04.551
Thank you for watching.
